; DB connection config consumed by Utils\Connectivity\Database.
;
; Sections are keyed by database name (the section header IS the database
; name), and the connector resolves a database to its [<dbname>] section:
;
;   $conn = Database::connectAs($dbname, $account)
;
; $account is one of this repo's service accounts (declared in
; etc/service-users.sql): `simox` (read-write on the primary, read on the
; replica) and `public` (read-only on the replica). The connector reads the
; password from the <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD key (uppercased account name +
; _PASSWORD); an empty value means a passwordless account. This repo is
; passwordless by policy — the security boundary is ZeroTier membership plus
; the source-IP host pin that bin/gen-service-users derives from
; etc/team.ini / etc/machines.ini.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only and is MANUALLY MAINTAINED by the
; consumer (private data, injected into etc/ by fetch-private-data — see
; doc/system/private-config.md). There is no generator anymore: `ema create
; srv/<name>-<GUID>` provisions the database's own MariaDB instance and
; prints the [<dbname>] section (SERVER/PORT/DBMS/MYSQL_UNIX_PORT) for the
; operator to record here (or `ema values <db>` recovers a lost record). The
; dev sandbox lives in var/sandbox/<name>-<guid>/reuter.ini (generated by
; 'ema sandbox srv/<name>-<GUID>'), not here.
;
; The <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD keys are manual, consumer-side credentials (recorded
; here by hand; empty = passwordless). bin/gen-service-users reconciles the
; accounts (create + drop stale) against etc/service-users.sql but does NOT
; write these keys back — this file is the manual source of truth.
;
; Two databases: `simo0` is the writable primary and `simo1` is its read-only
; replica (replication is established by ema's replica build — see
; doc/system/replica-bootstrap.md). Each has its own section below. `simo0`
; carries the `simox` password key only (`public` is never created there);
; `simo1` carries both (`simox` may also read it).
;
; Transport: the section is authoritative for the 'ema' CLI. When
; MYSQL_UNIX_PORT is set, ema connects via that socket (root/unix_socket
; auth); otherwise it uses SERVER/PORT over TCP. The app layer
; (Utils\Connectivity\Database) reads MYSQL_UNIX_PORT from .env, not from
; this file, so in prod it stays TCP-only (.env is MYSQL_*-free).

[simo0]
SERVER=10.147.x.10
PORT=3307
DBMS=mariadb
SIMOX_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock

[simo1]
SERVER=10.147.x.11
PORT=3308
DBMS=mariadb
SIMOX_PASSWORD=
PUBLIC_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock
